--- Finds the first element of a list satisfying a predicate.
---
--- @details
--- `find` takes `[pred, xs]` and returns the first `x` in `xs` for
--- which `pred(x)` is truthy, or `null` when no element matches. It is
--- the `comb`-surface spelling of `combinators.find`.
---
--- @example
--- `[x ~> x > 2, [1, 2, 3, 4]] >>> comb.find`
--- -- => 3
---
export find :: [pred, xs] ~> combinators.find(pred, xs)
